# Etiuda 2.x - this repo is public, and this file is the last thing standing between the
# folder and the internet.
#
# IT IS A BLOCKLIST, AND 1.x USED THE OPPOSITE. There the product was one HTML file, the repo
# published five files, and the ignore file ignored everything (`/*`) and named those five back
# in. Everything else in the folder was private by default. Here the source itself is the thing
# being published, so the default has to be "committed" and this file names the exceptions.
#
# The inversion has a cost, and it is worth stating plainly: an allowlist is safe against a
# filename nobody has thought of yet, and a blocklist is not. What pays for it is a naming
# convention, so that the patterns below have something to bite on. Keep to the convention and
# this file keeps working; drift from it and this file quietly stops protecting anything.
#
#   - A catalog lives at the root as `*-catalog.js` / `*-catalog.json`, or inside `catalogs/`,
#     and nowhere else. Source code that merely deals with catalogs is code: give it a plain
#     name (`catalog-loader.ts`, not `x-catalog.ts`) so it is not swept up here.
#   - Anything unfinished, exported, measured or screenshotted goes in `scratch/`.
#   - A secret is never a file in this tree at all. The patterns below are the second line,
#     not the first.
#
# Two checks, both cheap. `git status --ignored` shows what is being held back, and
# `git diff --cached --stat` before every commit shows what is going out. This file is a
# guard, not a reviewer, and `git add -f` walks straight past it.

# --- Catalogs -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A catalog is content, and content belongs to whoever wrote it. One is kept in this folder so
# the app can be run against something real; it is never committed, under this name or any
# other. To publish a demo catalog, name it back in with a `!` line and say in the commit
# message whose it is, which for a demo is nobody's.
#
# UNANCHORED ON PURPOSE, unlike every other pattern in this file. A leading slash would hold
# only for the root, and the engine sources sit in a subfolder that a browser will want a
# catalog beside. A catalog is a catalog at whatever depth it lands.
*-catalog.js
*-catalog.json
etiuda-catalog.js
catalogs/
# The one catalog here that is not somebody else's content: the 1.x demo, invented for Etiuda
# and published deliberately under v1/. Named back in as the block above says a demo is.
#
# THIS LINE IS READ BY THE SCAN. tools/pre-commit refuses any catalog-named path it finds in
# the index, and under v1/ it makes one exception: a path git reports NOT ignored, which is a
# `!` line here and nothing else. So this file and that scan agree by construction, and a
# second `!` in this block publishes a second demo without a second edit there. Deleting this
# line makes the scan refuse the tree, which is the right way round.
!/v1/sample-catalog.js
# A format 2 catalog is a `.ec` file, for etiuda catalog, and it is a catalog whatever it is
# called: the naming convention above holds for the old format only, so the extension is the
# pattern here. Unanchored for the same reason as the lines above it.
*.ec
# The second catalog that is nobody's: the sample the installer puts in the catalog folder on a
# first run, named back in exactly as the block above says a demo is. Chopin's letters, public
# domain, written for this purpose; it ships inside the asar, so it has to be in the tree.
!/shell/sample-catalog.ec

# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
.npmrc
/secrets/

# --- Build output and dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
# Reproducible from the source next door, and a signed artifact is distributed from a release
# rather than from the tree.
/node_modules/
/dist/
/build/
/out/
/release/
*.asar
*.log

# --- Scratch --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Probes, previews, screenshots, timings. Real work, none of it the product.
/scratch/
/previews/
*.tmp

# --- Local to one machine -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and agent configuration, and the unpublished notes that sit beside the public ones.
#
# `.claude/` is ignored for a harder reason than tidiness and it stays ignored. An agent role
# file may be linked into it from a private repository, and on Windows such a link commonly
# lands in git as an ordinary file holding the path it points at. Tracking this folder would
# publish that path. Nothing in this repository names or points at a private repository, and
# this is the line where that would happen by accident rather than on purpose. A development
# script worth publishing belongs in `tools/`, never in an exception carved out here.
/.claude/
/.vscode/
/.idea/
# `CLAUDE.md` is the same rule one level up: the working method is private, so the file is
# copied in from outside this tree, read by every session here, and committed by nobody.
# tests/README.md says where a fresh clone gets one.
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Transitional: 1.x is still on this disk ------------------------------------------------
# This folder was the 1.x working tree until the repositories were split, and the 1.x harness
# and release tooling are still sitting in it. None of it is part of 2.x and none of it is
# published: some of it names what is not ours to name, and some of it carries evaluation data
# taken from a real catalog. They are listed rather than left to the silence, because under a
# blocklist silence means "commit it".
#
# IF 2.x WANTS ONE OF THESE NAMES, delete its line here in the same commit that creates the
# file. Otherwise the new file is ignored and nothing says why.
#
# SEVEN OF THESE NAMES NOW EXIST TWICE, and no line below was touched to allow it. Every pattern
# here is anchored to the root, so tests/test.js was never ignored and the harness entered this
# repository on `git add tests/` alone, with nothing in this file deciding it. That is the
# blocklist's cost stated plainly: `tests/` is public and only the reviewer's eye put it there.
# The root copies stay ignored and stay 1.x. tests/README.md says which is which.
#
# WHAT STILL BITES INSIDE tests/ is the catalog block above, because it is unanchored: measured,
# tests/etiuda-catalog.js and tests/sample-catalog.js are both ignored at whatever depth. That is
# the one protection that travels, and it is why the harness keeps its fixtures outside the tree
# rather than relying on it.
/test.js
/smoke.js
/test-guards.py
/prepush-scan.py
/i18n-scan.js
/i18n-audit.js
/search-eval.js
/deadcode.js
/css-dead.js
/ghosts.js
/storage-keys.js
/catalog-edit.js
/comment-pass.js
/preview-kit.js
/verify-preview.js
/release.js
/pages-kick.js
/build-integrated.js
/TOOLS.md
/__pycache__/
